.TH HTTP_BODY 3
.SH NAME
http_body \- set the body of a request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_body(http* " h ", const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_body ()
appends
.I n
bytes at
.I x
to the body of the request that was started last. The length is only known when the
request is sent, it goes out as Content-Length. The function can be called several times to
build the body piece by piece; use
.BR http_chunked (3)
when the data should be sent while it is produced.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 if there is no request, the body was declared chunked, or the memory is short.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_chunked(3), http_post(3)
